// Curated in-game essentials. Advanced options remain available in the INI.
// Group order: Attendance, Soundscape, Broadcast; toggles precede numeric controls.
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Enabled","Dynamic Attendance","Let fans arrive late, leave early and take halftime breaks as the game unfolds.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ArrivalsEnabled","Fans Arriving After Kickoff","Start with some fans still outside and let them arrive during the first quarter, up to the expected peak crowd.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTrafficEnabled","Beat the Traffic Departures","Let fans leave faster in a home blowout: 17+ deficits start in the last third of Q4, or gently in the last half for 28+. With 12-minute quarters, that means 4:00 or a gentle 6:00 start.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Profile","Fan Patience","Automatic chooses patience from the matchup and weather. Normal uses standard departures; Patient Fans slows departures; Bad Weather makes fans leave sooner.",0,0,3,Kind::Profile},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"StartPercent","Ordinary Opening Crowd (%)","Opening fraction of expected peak for an average-support program. School support nudges this within 40-50%; night, marquee games and weather can adjust it. Affects future fresh games.",45.0,40.0,50.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateSchoolStartPercent","Late-Arriving Schools: Start (%)","Opening fraction of expected peak for UCLA, Miami (FL), Georgia Tech, Maryland and Utah. Higher means more fans at kickoff. Night, marquee games and weather can adjust it. Affects future fresh games.",40.0,40.0,50.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BigGameBonus","Big Game Opening Bonus (points)","Extra opening fans for two Top25 teams, or a rivalry with either team Top25 or both Top50. Regular openings remain capped at 70% of expected peak. Postseason uses its separate protected opening range.",7.0,0.0,7.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FinishPercentOfQuarter","Arrivals Finish: Through Q1 (%)","How far through Q1 ordinary schools finish arriving. Higher means later; 50 means halfway through Q1. Marquee, severe-late and postseason games use their separate deadlines. Affects future fresh games.",50.0,10.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FormulaStrength","Fans Leaving Early (%)","Overall strength of departures caused by the score, time and matchup. Higher makes more fans leave; lower keeps more fans. 100 is normal; 0 turns off these departures. Halftime and late-score departures have separate controls.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"HalftimeSeatBreakStrength","Fans Away at Halftime (%)","How many fans temporarily leave their seats around halftime. Higher means more empty seats; lower means fewer. 100 is normal strength; 0 turns this off. Fans who stay return early in Q3.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Enabled","Crowd Sound Effects","Adjust crowd excitement to the occupied seats and enable added crowd sounds. Turning this on after starting the game with it off requires a game restart.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LayeredAtmosphereEnabled","Added Crowd Atmosphere","Enable added crowd reactions. Quieter games get simple sounds; qualifying situations and fuller stadiums can also get roars, excitement, volume boosts and camera reactions.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OpeningAtmosphere","Opening Game Atmosphere","Add crowd buildup during the stadium introduction and early first quarter. Big games can qualify from 50% fullness before the normal requirement gradually returns.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PlayCallAtmosphere","Play Selection Atmosphere","Add crowd roars and rising anticipation during play selection, plus ordinary successful-play reactions. Special cheers are for the home offense; the away offense gets roars and swells.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OvertimeAtmosphere","Overtime Crowd Atmosphere","Keep added crowd energy going between snaps during qualifying overtime situations. Stadium fullness requirements still apply.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"UpsetWatchAtmosphere","Upset Watch Crowd Sounds","Build crowd excitement from Q2 onward when a home underdog threatens a Top 25 visitor. Needs at least 50% stadium fullness. At neutral sites, either underdog can qualify.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"DuringPlayReactionsEnabled","Live Play Crowd Reactions","Add sounds for confirmed long gains, takeaways, sacks, defensive breakups and returns. Below the atmosphere requirement these are sound-only; shake and fuller layers still require enough fans.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SkillMoveReactions","Skill Move and Big Hit Reactions","Add crowd reactions to successful skill moves and big hits. Spins, jukes and regular broken tackles use sound only; trucks and hurdles can add gentle movement. Hit-stick shake requires a third- or fourth-down stop.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PassFlightAnticipation","Crowd Swell During Passes","Let the crowd build anticipation while a qualifying pass is in the air, then settle after the catch or incompletion. Requires Live Play Crowd Reactions.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SituationalCrowdReactions","Crowd Cheers and Disappointment","Add disappointment for costly home mistakes, deep visitor catches and opponent scores, plus cheers for defensive plays. Quieter games keep these sound-only.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"WinningEruptions","Major Celebrations","Use the biggest crowd celebration for special plays: the first touchdown in the opening two plays, decisive late scores, overtime winners and game-sealing takeaways. Long touchdowns in close games get a modest touchdown boost instead.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Soundscape",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"NativeQuietingStrengthPercent","Small Crowd Excitement Reduction (%)","How much calmer the background crowd becomes as seats empty. Higher makes the bed calmer; lower preserves more native excitement. Big-play peaks can rise above the bed ceiling. 0 turns this off; changes fade gradually.",100.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PauseMenuFullness","Show Fullness in Pause Menu","Show Stadium Fullness beside Resume in the pause menu. This is the share of seats filled, updated when the menu opens. A dash means the measurement is not ready.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CameraShake","Added Camera Shake","Enable all camera shake added by the mod. The game's Dynamic Camera Effects setting must also be On.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"ExtraReplaysEnabled","Additional Replays","Allow the mod to request extra replays after plays. The game can still show its own replays when this is off.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"FullScreenBigPlays","Full-Screen Big Play Replays","Encourage full-screen replays for big plays. The game's usual skip controls still work.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"InsetAfterRoutinePlays","Small Replays After Routine Plays","Allow small replay windows during play selection after ordinary runs and completions.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DefensiveHighlights","Defensive Play Replays","Allow extra replay opportunities after sacks and tackles for loss, while keeping interception and lost-fumble highlights.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"FullScreenMinimumYards","Full-Screen Replay: Minimum Yards","Gain needed for an added full-screen big-play replay opportunity. Higher favors longer plays; lower lets shorter plays qualify. The game still decides whether to show the replay.",15.0,10.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"OrdinaryShakeStrengthPercent","Normal Play Selection Shake (%)","Maximum added shake during ordinary play selection. Higher gives stronger movement; lower gives gentler movement. 0 turns this type off. Pre-punt buildup uses half this strength. Camera zoom is accounted for.",5.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CriticalShakeStrengthPercent","Critical Down Shake (%)","Maximum added shake before qualifying third and fourth downs in close games. Higher makes it stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns this type off. Home-offense buildup is 15% gentler than the base range. Fullness requirements still apply.",10.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DuringPlayShakeStrengthPercent","Live Play Shake (%)","Shake for long gains, interceptions, sacks and forced fumbles. Higher makes it stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns it off. Kick/punt returns build from 30 yards to this strength at 40. Fumble pickups add no shake.",10.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeStrengthPercent","Touchdown Shake: Sustained (%)","Strength of touchdown celebrations. Higher makes the shake stronger; lower makes it gentler. An existing play reaction builds to this level. 0 turns off touchdown shake.",15.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeStrengthPercent","Major Celebration: Sustained (%)","Strength of the biggest celebrations, such as decisive winning plays. Higher makes the shake stronger; lower makes it gentler. An existing reaction builds to this level. 0 turns this shake off.",22.5,0.0,100.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Broadcast",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CannonShakeStrengthPercent","Stadium Cannon Shake (%)","Shake when a stadium cannon fires, independent of Live Play Shake. Higher makes the blast stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns cannon shake off without changing its sound. Works at any crowd fullness and respects Dynamic Camera Effects.",15.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
